en":[{"type":"text","value":"Render lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter creates one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartRuntime"},{"type":"text","value":" for each component instance and asks the\nselected renderer for initial markup in TSRX. After layout:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLayoutEffect"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the initial runtime is passed through"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a later layout effect forwards memoized host options"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"subsequent Octane updates call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.update"},{"type":"text","value":"; a new definition identity\nrebuilds the scene"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"cleanup destroys the host and all browser-owned behavior"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The inner chart surface is memoized after its first output. The shared host\npaints later scenes directly into the selected surface. Memoize definitions\nthat capture component values with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useMemo"},{"type":"text","value":"; module-scope definitions need no\ncomponent memoization."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ssr-and-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR and hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default Node target renders the complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-surface"},{"type":"text","value":", and accessible SVG at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":". The browser target\nhydrates the same structure before mounting the host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Canvas entry renders a deterministic named root and five "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncanvases on the server: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It paints no server pixels. The browser adopts the elements, paints\nafter mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip, and selection\nhost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the browser adopts every child\nsurface."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep data, definitions, scale domains, custom renderers, and dimensions\ndeterministic between server and browser. The adapter generates a sanitized\nresource prefix from Octane's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useId()"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"},{"type":"text","value":" is absent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabIndex"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" on both targets. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard: false"},{"type":"text","value":" forces it to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both targets. Custom\nserializers must preserve the same resources; see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"sizing-and-layout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sizing and layout"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rendered structure is:"}]},{"type":"code","value":".ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The outer host uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"position: relative"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Props"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outer host behavior"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scene behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":", fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; fixed height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"container width × fixed height"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed CSS dimensions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"same fixed scene dimensions"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed width and CSS ratio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fixed width divided by ratio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"positive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":", no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; CSS aspect ratio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"measured width divided by ratio"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"neither "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height: 320px"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"measured width × 320"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"640"},{"type":"text","value":". A fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" takes precedence over\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":"; nonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default\nheight. Responsive measurement and inherited font relayout are shared with the vanilla\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DOM host"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"class-and-style","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane-specific presentation props apply to the outer host:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  class=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{\n    minHeight: 240,\n    color: 'var(--foreground)',\n  }}\n/>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" is appended after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, string | number | undefined>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"styles are spread after adapter sizing, so they can override position,\nwidth, height, or aspect ratio."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not conflict a fixed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" prop with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style.width"},{"type":"text","value":". The style changes the\nouter CSS box while the prop continues to lock scene width. A custom\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style.height"},{"type":"text","value":" remains live when both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aspectRatio"},{"type":"text","value":" are absent.\nEither sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS height when supplied."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The core renderer's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"},{"type":"text","value":" option applies to a directly rendered surface,\nnot the Octane outer host."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definition-and-option-identity","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition and option identity"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep fixed definitions outside component execution. Keep one dynamic\ndefinition stable until a captured application value changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter memoizes host options from semantic props. Callback functions are\nheld in refs, so changing only a callback does not rebuild the option object\nand the live wrapper still calls the latest function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition identity is core behavior; see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" portals Octane output into the core-owned tooltip body. Its\ncontext contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss"},{"type":"text","value":".\nInclude "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":" to retain native rows and swatches. The shared host owns\nfocus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and dismissal;\nOctane owns the returned component lifecycle."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"core-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Core boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter does not redefine chart grammar or data algorithms. Read\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scales"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for injected primitives and\nthe "},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"core API reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for marks, interaction,\nrenderers, and extension contracts."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"public-exports","text":"Public exports","level":2},{"id":"render-lifecycle","text":"Render lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"ssr-and-hydration","text":"SSR and hydration","level":2},{"id":"sizing-and-layout","text":"Sizing and layout","level":2},{"id":"class-and-style","text":"class and style","level":2},{"id":"definition-and-option-identity","text":"Definition and option identity","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2},{"id":"core-boundary","text":"Core boundary","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`@tanstack/charts/octane` is the native TSRX lifecycle and SSR adapter around\n`@tanstack/charts`. Definitions, scenes, responsive layout, rendering,\ninteraction, and animation remain framework-neutral.\n\n## Public exports\n\n```ts\nexport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\n\nexport type {\n  ChartCommonProps,\n  ChartProps,\n  ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext,\n  ChartDefinition,\n  ChartPoint,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\n```\n\nChoose Canvas or an application-supplied renderer through an explicit\nsubpath:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as CanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas'\nimport { Chart as RendererChart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane/core'\n```\n\nThe default `Chart` remains SVG-based. `CanvasChart` selects the optional\nbuilt-in renderer; `RendererChart` requires a `renderer` prop. A definition\ncan still import `canvasChartRenderer` and assign it to selected marks, which\nmakes the default component render an ordered mixed surface.\n\nThe package export map supplies a browser build for browser bundlers and a\nseparate Node build for the `node` condition.\n\n## Render lifecycle\n\nThe adapter creates one `ChartRuntime` for each component instance and asks the\nselected renderer for initial markup in TSRX. After layout:\n\n1. `useLayoutEffect` mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface\n2. the initial runtime is passed through\n3. a later layout effect forwards memoized host options\n4. subsequent Octane updates call `host.update`; a new definition identity\n   rebuilds the scene\n5. cleanup destroys the host and all browser-owned behavior\n\nThe inner chart surface is memoized after its first output. The shared host\npaints later scenes directly into the selected surface. Memoize definitions\nthat capture component values with `useMemo`; module-scope definitions need no\ncomponent memoization.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\nThe default Node target renders the complete `.ts-chart-host`,\n`.ts-chart-surface`, and accessible SVG at `initialWidth`. The browser target\nhydrates the same structure before mounting the host.\n\nThe Canvas entry renders a deterministic named root and five `aria-hidden`\ncanvases on the server: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It paints no server pixels. The browser adopts the elements, paints\nafter mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip, and selection\nhost.\n\nA default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the browser adopts every child\nsurface.\n\nKeep data, definitions, scale domains, custom renderers, and dimensions\ndeterministic between server and browser. The adapter generates a sanitized\nresource prefix from Octane's `useId()` when `idPrefix` is absent.\n\n`tabIndex` defaults to `0` on both targets. `keyboard: false` forces it to\n`-1`.\n\nThe default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both targets. Custom\nserializers must preserve the same resources; see\n[Rendering and export](../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources).\n\n## Sizing and layout\n\nThe rendered structure is:\n\n```text\n.ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers\n```\n\nThe outer host uses `position: relative`.\n\n| Props                               | Outer host behavior             | Scene behavior                  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| no `width`, fixed `height`          | `width: 100%`; fixed height     | container width × fixed height  |\n| fixed `width` and `height`          | fixed CSS dimensions            | same fixed scene dimensions     |\n| fixed `width` and `aspectRatio`     | fixed width and CSS ratio       | fixed width divided by ratio    |\n| positive `aspectRatio`, no `height` | `width: 100%`; CSS aspect ratio | measured width divided by ratio |\n| neither `height` nor `aspectRatio`  | `width: 100%`; `height: 320px`  | measured width × 320            |\n\n`initialWidth` defaults to `640`. A fixed `height` takes precedence over\n`aspectRatio`; nonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default\nheight. Responsive measurement and inherited font relayout are shared with the vanilla\n[DOM host](../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing).\n\n## `class` and `style`\n\nOctane-specific presentation props apply to the outer host:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  class=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{\n    minHeight: 240,\n    color: 'var(--foreground)',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n- `class` is appended after `ts-chart-host`.\n- `style` is `Record<string, string | number | undefined>`.\n- styles are spread after adapter sizing, so they can override position,\n  width, height, or aspect ratio.\n\nDo not conflict a fixed `width` prop with `style.width`. The style changes the\nouter CSS box while the prop continues to lock scene width. A custom\n`style.height` remains live when both `height` and `aspectRatio` are absent.\nEither sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS height when supplied.\n\nThe core renderer's `className` option applies to a directly rendered surface,\nnot the Octane outer host.\n\n## Definition and option identity\n\nKeep fixed definitions outside component execution. Keep one dynamic\ndefinition stable until a captured application value changes.\n\nThe adapter memoizes host options from semantic props. Callback functions are\nheld in refs, so changing only a callback does not rebuild the option object\nand the live wrapper still calls the latest function.\n\nDefinition identity is core behavior; see\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n`renderTooltipBody` portals Octane output into the core-owned tooltip body. Its\ncontext contains `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and `dismiss`.\nInclude `defaultBody` to retain native rows and swatches. The shared host owns\nfocus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and dismissal;\nOctane owns the returned component lifecycle.\n\n## Core boundary\n\nThe adapter does not redefine chart grammar or data algorithms. Read\n[Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) for injected primitives and\nthe [core API reference](../../reference/index.md) for marks, interaction,\nrenderers, and extension contracts.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Octane Adapter\ndescription: Understand the native TSRX lifecycle, conditional SSR target, hydration, sizing, class, and style behavior around the shared chart host.\n---\n\n`@tanstack/charts/octane` is the native TSRX lifecycle and SSR adapter around\n`@tanstack/charts`. Definitions, scenes, responsive layout, rendering,\ninteraction, and animation remain framework-neutral.\n\n## Public exports\n\n```ts\nexport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\n\nexport type {\n  ChartCommonProps,\n  ChartProps,\n  ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext,\n  ChartDefinition,\n  ChartPoint,\n} from '@tanstack/charts/octane'\n```\n\nChoose Canvas or an application-supplied renderer through an explicit\nsubpath:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Chart as CanvasChart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane/canvas'\nimport { Chart as RendererChart } from '@tanstack/charts/octane/core'\n```\n\nThe default `Chart` remains SVG-based. `CanvasChart` selects the optional\nbuilt-in renderer; `RendererChart` requires a `renderer` prop. A definition\ncan still import `canvasChartRenderer` and assign it to selected marks, which\nmakes the default component render an ordered mixed surface.\n\nThe package export map supplies a browser build for browser bundlers and a\nseparate Node build for the `node` condition.\n\n## Render lifecycle\n\nThe adapter creates one `ChartRuntime` for each component instance and asks the\nselected renderer for initial markup in TSRX. After layout:\n\n1. `useLayoutEffect` mounts the shared DOM host into the existing chart surface\n2. the initial runtime is passed through\n3. a later layout effect forwards memoized host options\n4. subsequent Octane updates call `host.update`; a new definition identity\n   rebuilds the scene\n5. cleanup destroys the host and all browser-owned behavior\n\nThe inner chart surface is memoized after its first output. The shared host\npaints later scenes directly into the selected surface. Memoize definitions\nthat capture component values with `useMemo`; module-scope definitions need no\ncomponent memoization.\n\n## SSR and hydration\n\nThe default Node target renders the complete `.ts-chart-host`,\n`.ts-chart-surface`, and accessible SVG at `initialWidth`. The browser target\nhydrates the same structure before mounting the host.\n\nThe Canvas entry renders a deterministic named root and five `aria-hidden`\ncanvases on the server: one hidden stable base bitmap and four live paint\nlayers. It paints no server pixels. The browser adopts the elements, paints\nafter mount, and attaches the same focus, keyboard, tooltip, and selection\nhost.\n\nA default chart with selected Canvas marks emits one mixed root containing\nordered SVG markup and Canvas shells. SVG marks are visible in the server\nresponse, Canvas pixels appear after mount, and the browser adopts every child\nsurface.\n\nKeep data, definitions, scale domains, custom renderers, and dimensions\ndeterministic between server and browser. The adapter generates a sanitized\nresource prefix from Octane's `useId()` when `idPrefix` is absent.\n\n`tabIndex` defaults to `0` on both targets. `keyboard: false` forces it to\n`-1`.\n\nThe default SVG renderer emits gradients and clipping on both targets. Custom\nserializers must preserve the same resources; see\n[Rendering and export](../../reference/rendering-and-export.md#svg-resources).\n\n## Sizing and layout\n\nThe rendered structure is:\n\n```text\n.ts-chart-host\n  .ts-chart-surface\n    svg.ts-chart | div.ts-chart-canvas | div.ts-chart-layers\n```\n\nThe outer host uses `position: relative`.\n\n| Props                               | Outer host behavior             | Scene behavior                  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| no `width`, fixed `height`          | `width: 100%`; fixed height     | container width × fixed height  |\n| fixed `width` and `height`          | fixed CSS dimensions            | same fixed scene dimensions     |\n| fixed `width` and `aspectRatio`     | fixed width and CSS ratio       | fixed width divided by ratio    |\n| positive `aspectRatio`, no `height` | `width: 100%`; CSS aspect ratio | measured width divided by ratio |\n| neither `height` nor `aspectRatio`  | `width: 100%`; `height: 320px`  | measured width × 320            |\n\n`initialWidth` defaults to `640`. A fixed `height` takes precedence over\n`aspectRatio`; nonpositive and nonfinite ratios fall back to the default\nheight. Responsive measurement and inherited font relayout are shared with the vanilla\n[DOM host](../../reference/dom-host.md#responsive-sizing).\n\n## `class` and `style`\n\nOctane-specific presentation props apply to the outer host:\n\n```tsx\n<Chart\n  definition={definition}\n  ariaLabel=\"Revenue\"\n  class=\"dashboard-chart\"\n  style={{\n    minHeight: 240,\n    color: 'var(--foreground)',\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n- `class` is appended after `ts-chart-host`.\n- `style` is `Record<string, string | number | undefined>`.\n- styles are spread after adapter sizing, so they can override position,\n  width, height, or aspect ratio.\n\nDo not conflict a fixed `width` prop with `style.width`. The style changes the\nouter CSS box while the prop continues to lock scene width. A custom\n`style.height` remains live when both `height` and `aspectRatio` are absent.\nEither sizing prop stays authoritative over CSS height when supplied.\n\nThe core renderer's `className` option applies to a directly rendered surface,\nnot the Octane outer host.\n\n## Definition and option identity\n\nKeep fixed definitions outside component execution. Keep one dynamic\ndefinition stable until a captured application value changes.\n\nThe adapter memoizes host options from semantic props. Callback functions are\nheld in refs, so changing only a callback does not rebuild the option object\nand the live wrapper still calls the latest function.\n\nDefinition identity is core behavior; see\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\n`renderTooltipBody` portals Octane output into the core-owned tooltip body. Its\ncontext contains `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and `dismiss`.\nInclude `defaultBody` to retain native rows and swatches. The shared host owns\nfocus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and dismissal;\nOctane owns the returned component lifecycle.\n\n## Core boundary\n\nThe adapter does not redefine chart grammar or data algorithms. Read\n[Scales](../../concepts/scales-and-d3.md) for injected primitives and\nthe [core API reference](../../reference/index.md) for marks, interaction,\nrenderers, and extension contracts.\n"}
